# Non-idempotent under prettier 3.9.4: these editor lit-templates embed TS
# casts inside interpolated expressions (e.g. `${(e.target as
# HTMLInputElement)...}`) and their indentation keeps drifting across
# repeated `--write` passes instead of converging on the first pass (4
# passes needed from a clean baseline; verified 2026-09-10). A pre-commit
# hook only runs `--write` once, so these files would be left in a
# non-canonical state that a `--check` step would then flag as dirty even
# right after the hook "fixed" them. Tracked upstream: #345.
